    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One of my concerns is the sheer volume of unrestored, uncatalogued materials that came in with this batch. They are currently just sitting in various crates and are a bit of a mess. If we start with DDC, do you think we'll run into issues with \"bottlenecks\" once the collection grows and the lack of specific categories starts causing too much clutter or confusion in the system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, starting with DDC on a large, messy collection risks significant bottlenecks as the volume increases and collection gaps appear. DDC can become overly general for highly specific, unique manuscripts, forcing you to use broad categories that fail to accurately reflect the material's content. In such scenarios, the rigid numerical structure may not provide the necessary fine-grained distinctions, leading to classification clutter and discovery issues down the line.",
      "source": "target",
